      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Although further work is needed to improve spatial resolution and flow contrast as well as to lessen dependence on a regular cardiac rhythm, the potential clinical utility of MR coronary angiography is substantial. For the first time, information regarding coronary artery anatomy can be acquired in a completely noninvasive manner."},
